WEBVTT

00:09:29.281 --> 00:09:31.427
looked at Europe,
saw these things, and said,

00:09:31.451 --> 00:09:33.040
"Why don't we have these things?"

00:09:33.064 --> 00:09:35.081
And they looked back at Islamic tradition,

00:09:35.105 --> 00:09:37.517
and saw that there are
problematic aspects,

00:09:37.541 --> 00:09:41.290
but they're not the core of the religion,
so maybe they can be re-understood,

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:43.895
and the Koran can be reread
in the modern world.

00:09:44.392 --> 00:09:49.158
That trend is generally called
Islamic modernism,

00:09:49.281 --> 00:09:52.258
and it was advanced
by intellectuals and statesmen,

00:09:52.282 --> 00:09:54.376
not just as an intellectual idea, though,

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.113
but also as a political program.

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:58.324
And that's why, actually,
in the 19th century,

00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:01.940
the Ottoman Empire, which then
covered the whole Middle East,